In HTTP 1, one get is there and something error there. So it has to wait till second get will succeed. Then the third one goes, right? In HTTP 2 with quick, those are all parallel with different quick. If that is error,

437
01:38:39,412 --> 01:38:45,592
It may go, but meanwhile, 3rd GET may receive, right?

438
01:38:45,592 --> 01:38:50,631
Then, at the receiver side, it's reassembled.

439
01:38:50,631 --> 01:38:57,032
And as you can see, HTTP2 with QUIC, no head of line blocking.

